    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` run is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure-based membership level rule in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/MembershipLevel.java`.\n\n**The change:** Previously `MembershipLevel.of(...)` hard-capped the level at 3 via `Math.min(level, MAX)` \u2014 level 4 was documented as \"reserved for tenure\" but was never actually reachable. Now:\n\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, `+1` for a present email, `+1` for `namesakeCount == 0`) are still capped at `MAX = 3`.\n- A new tenure factor adds `+1` (reaching level 4) only when the owner's `registrationDate` is more than 365 days in the past (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now) > 365`).\n- A null `registrationDate` counts as zero tenure.\n\n**Why this satisfies the spec:** A newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to (business-day-adjusted) today, so tenure is 0 and the tenure factor never fires \u2014 a new owner is capped at level 3. Level 4 is now genuinely gated on tenure > 365 days, which only an aged owner can meet. The `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` acceptance test (new owner with email, `namesakeCount` 0, 3-member household \u2192 level 3) passes, as does the full suite.",
